---
import Layout from '../../studio/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { mailto, studio } from '../../apps/registry';

const title = 'Terms of Service — Paperdot';
const description = 'Terms of Service for Paperdot (com.yanerapps.paperdot), a daily journal and planner for Android by Yaner Apps.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="prose">
    <nav aria-label="Paperdot navigation" class="product-nav">
      Paperdot <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Terms
      <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/paperdot/privacy">Privacy</a><span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/paperdot/support">Support</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="prose-header">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="lede">Paperdot for Android (<code>com.yanerapps.paperdot</code>)</p>
      <div class="meta">
        <span>Effective: from Paperdot&rsquo;s release on Google Play</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      These terms govern your use of the Paperdot Android application ("the app"), made by Yaner Yang, publishing
      as Yaner Apps ("we", "us"). By installing or using the app you agree to them. If you do not agree, do not use
      the app. How the app handles data is described separately in the <a href="/paperdot/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="card">
      <p><strong>In short:</strong> Paperdot is a journal that keeps everything on your device. Your journal is
      yours; we never see it, so we cannot recover it, and keeping backups is up to you. Optional Paperdot Sync
      stores it end-to-end encrypted, which still means we cannot read or recover it without your passphrase or
      recovery key. Pro and Sync are optional and sold and billed by Google Play. Subscriptions renew automatically until you
      cancel; Lifetime Pro is paid once. When they end nothing in your journal is changed or deleted. The app is provided as is, and our liability is limited as far as the law allows.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. What Paperdot does</h2>
    <p>
      Paperdot is a daily journal and planner for rapid logging: tasks, events and notes in daily, monthly and
      future logs, with collections, habit trackers, reminders and a guided review of open tasks. It needs Android
      8.0 or later and works without an account or a network connection; only the optional Paperdot Sync needs a
      Google sign-in and a connection. If you allow it, it reads the calendars
      you choose to show their events next to your logs; it never creates or changes calendar events.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Your content</h2>
    <p>
      Everything you write in Paperdot belongs to you. We claim no rights to it. Without Sync we never receive it. With
      Sync we store it only end-to-end encrypted, which we cannot read (see the <a href="/paperdot/privacy">privacy
      policy</a>). You are responsible for what you write and for keeping it lawful.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Backups and data loss</h2>
    <p>
      Without Sync, your journal exists only on your device, so we cannot recover it if it is lost, for example when you uninstall
      the app, clear its data, reset or lose the device, or use "Delete all data". Make regular backups
      (<code>.paperdot.json</code>) in <strong>Profile &rarr; Back up &amp; restore</strong> and keep them somewhere
      safe. Backup and export files are not encrypted, so anyone who gets one can read it. Restoring a backup
      replaces the journal on the device; the app saves a copy of the current journal first. App lock keeps casual
      eyes out of the app; it does not encrypt your journal, and it does not hide reminders or the home screen widget.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Reminders and calendar</h2>
    <p>
      Reminders are delivered by Android. The system, battery savers, Do Not Disturb or a device restart can delay
      or block them, so do not rely on Paperdot alone for anything where a missed reminder could cause harm, such as
      medication or safety. Calendar events are shown as Android reports them; we do not check their accuracy.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Licence</h2>
    <p>
      We grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and use the app on
      Android devices you own or control, for your own purposes, in line with these terms and the Google Play Terms
      of Service. You may not copy, resell, sublicense or redistribute the app, remove its notices, tamper with its
      subscription checks, or reverse engineer it except where the law expressly allows it. The app, its name, icon
      and design remain ours. The fonts bundled with the app are used under their own licences, listed in the app
      under <strong>Profile &rarr; About</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Free version and Pro</h2>
    <p>
      Paperdot is free to download, and every journal feature works in the free version. Paperdot Pro is optional and
      unlocks more, either as a subscription or as Lifetime Pro, bought once; both unlock the same features.
    </p>
    <p>
      The current features and price of each Pro plan are shown in the
      app before you buy; prices come from Google Play in your local currency. They may change over time. A price
      change for an existing subscription follows Google Play's rules, including any notice and consent Google Play
      requires.
    </p>
    <h3>Billing, trial and renewal</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Pro is sold and billed by Google Play and charged to the payment method in your Google account. We never see your payment details.</li>
      <li>Lifetime Pro is paid once and never renews.</li>
      <li>Each subscription plan renews automatically at the end of its period, at the then-current price, unless you cancel before the renewal date.</li>
      <li>If a plan includes a free trial, its length is shown before you confirm. Unless you cancel before the trial ends, the plan's price is charged when it ends.</li>
      <li>If your payment is pending, Pro starts once Google Play confirms the payment.</li>
      <li>Switching between plans is handled by Google Play, which credits or charges the difference under its own rules.</li>
      <li>Buying Lifetime Pro does not cancel a Pro subscription you already have. Cancel it in Google Play so you are not charged again; the app reminds you.</li>
      <li>The app confirms Pro with Google Play. If it cannot reach Google Play, Pro keeps working for a limited time since the last confirmation, after which the app shows the free version until it can check again.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Cancelling and refunds</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        You can cancel at any time in <strong>Profile &rarr; Paperdot Pro &rarr; Manage subscription</strong>, in the
        Google Play app under <strong>Profile &rarr; Payments &amp; subscriptions &rarr; Subscriptions</strong>, or at
        <a href="https://play.google.com/store/account/subscriptions" rel="noopener" target="_blank">play.google.com/store/account/subscriptions</a>.
        Uninstalling the app does not cancel a subscription.
      </li>
      <li>
        After you cancel a subscription, Pro stays active until the end of the period you have paid for. When Pro ends, for whatever
        reason, nothing in your journal is changed or deleted; only Pro features stop being available. Backups and
        Markdown export always stay free.
      </li>
      <li>
        Refunds are handled by Google Play under its
        <a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/2479637" rel="noopener" target="_blank">refund policy</a>.
        If something went wrong with a purchase, write to us as well and we will help where we can. Nothing in these
        terms limits any right of withdrawal or refund that consumer law gives you.
      </li>
      <li>Pro is tied to the Google account that bought it, not to a device. Use <strong>Restore purchases</strong> in the app after a reinstall or on a new device signed in to the same account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6a. Paperdot Sync</h2>
    <p>
      Paperdot Sync is a separate, optional yearly subscription that keeps your journal the same on your devices. It is
      sold and billed by Google Play like Pro, with the same renewal, trial, cancelling and refund terms as above; Sync
      and Pro do not include each other. To use it you sign in with Google and choose a sync passphrase.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your journal is encrypted on your device before it is uploaded. We cannot read it, so <strong>if you forget your sync passphrase and lose your recovery key, nobody can recover what is synced</strong>. The journal on your devices is not affected.</li>
      <li>Sync is tied to your Paperdot account, not to a device: buy it once and it works on every Android device signed in to that account.</li>
      <li>When Sync ends, uploading stops; your journal on your devices is not changed, and you can still download and delete your synced data. We may delete synced data 180 days after Sync ended, after telling you in the app 30 and 7 days before.</li>
      <li>You can delete your account in the app (<strong>Profile &rarr; Sync &rarr; Delete account</strong>) or as described at <a href="/paperdot/delete-account">yanerapps.com/paperdot/delete-account</a>. Deleting the account does not cancel the subscription; cancel it in Google Play.</li>
      <li>Each account can hold up to 50,000 synced records; the app warns you before you get close.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Availability and changes to the app</h2>
    <p>
      We may update, change or remove features, and the app may stop working in part or in full because of changes
      to Android, Google Play or your device that we do not control. We will try to keep Pro features working for
      the period you have paid for. If we stop offering Pro, existing subscribers keep it until the end of their
      current period and it will not renew, and Lifetime Pro keeps the Pro features it unlocked.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, the app is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind,
      express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement, or that it will work on any
      particular device or Android version, without interruption, without error or without loss of data.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential or
      punitive damages, or for any loss of data, profits or opportunities, including a lost journal or a missed
      reminder, arising from your use of or inability to use the app. Our total liability for all claims relating to
      the app is limited to the amount you paid us for the app in the 12 months before the claim, or, if you paid
      nothing, to zero.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability that cannot be excluded or limited by law, such as
      liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for intent or gross negligence, and
      nothing affects the statutory rights you have as a consumer, including those under the consumer protection
      laws of the EEA and the United Kingdom.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Ending these terms</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop using the app at any time by uninstalling it, after cancelling any subscription in Google Play.
      If you seriously breach these terms, your licence ends. Sections 2, 3 and 8 to 11 continue to apply after that.
    </p>

    <h2>11. General</h2>
    <p>
      If a provision of these terms is found invalid, the rest remain in effect. Our not enforcing a provision is not
      a waiver of it. These terms, together with the privacy policy, are the whole agreement between you and us about
      the app. Where the law of your country of residence gives you mandatory consumer protections, they apply in
      addition to these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      If these terms change, the updated version is published on this page with a new date. Material changes will
      also be noted in the app's release notes. Continuing to use the app after a change means you accept the updated
      terms.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Yaner Apps &mdash; <a href={mailto('Paperdot terms')}>{studio.email}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
